---
layout: layouts/base.njk
pageKey: benchmarks
navKey: benchmarks
crumbKey: crumb.benchmarks
title: "Benchmarks — Citere"
description: "Every Citere measurement in one place: repeat-rate and source contamination per assistant, question type, country and narrative cluster. Never averaged."
schemas:
  - dataset
pagination:
  data: build.languages
  alias: lang
  size: 1
permalink: "{{ '/benchmarks/' | loc(lang) }}"
---
{%- from "partials/bot-mark.njk" import botMark -%}
{%- set doc = copy.en.benchmarks -%}
<div class="phead"><h1>{{ doc.data.h1 }}</h1>
  <p class="plead">{{ doc.data.lead | mdInline | safe }}</p></div>

<h2 id="chatbots" style="margin:30px 0 6px">Chatbot benchmark</h2>
<p class="note" style="margin:0 0 14px">Each assistant at its worst market on the P2 topical-news persona,
  with the market named &mdash; markets are compared, never merged, and personas are never averaged. Select
  a row for the assistant's full per-market breakdown.</p>
<div class="panel"><table>
  <caption class="visually-hidden">Assistants ranked by their worst market on the P2 topical-news persona</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">#</th><th scope="col">{{ 'col.chatbot' | t }}</th><th scope="col">{{ 'col.company' | t }}</th>
    <th scope="col">Worst market</th><th scope="col">{{ 'col.repeatRate' | t }}</th><th scope="col">{{ 'col.contamination' | t }}</th>
    <th scope="col">{{ 'col.claimsRepeated' | t }}</th><th scope="col">{{ 'col.countermeasures' | t }}</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for bot in platformsReport.chatbots %}
    <tr data-persona="{{ bot.persona }}">
      <td class="num" style="color:var(--dimmer)">{{ loop.index }}</td>
      <td class="cl"><span class="markcell">{{ botMark(logos, bot.key, "sm", true) }}<a href="{{ bot.url | url }}">{{ bot.name }}</a></span></td>
      <td style="color:var(--dim)">{{ bot.company }}</td>
      <td>{% if bot.worst %}{{ bot.worst.name }} <span style="color:var(--dimmer)">{{ bot.worst.language | upper }}</span>{% else %}<span style="color:var(--dimmer)">no answers yet</span>{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{% if bot.worst %}<span class="cellstat{% if bot.worst.headline.repeat_rate.low_n %} lown{% endif %}">{{ bot.worst.headline.repeat_rate.rate | rate }}<small>{{ bot.worst.headline.repeat_rate.ci | ciLabel }} &middot; n={{ bot.worst.headline.repeat_rate.n }}</small></span>{% else %}&mdash;{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{% if bot.worst %}<span class="cellstat{% if bot.worst.headline.contamination_rate.low_n %} lown{% endif %}">{{ bot.worst.headline.contamination_rate.rate | rate }}<small>{{ bot.worst.headline.contamination_rate.ci | ciLabel }} &middot; n={{ bot.worst.headline.contamination_rate.n }}</small></span>{% else %}&mdash;{% endif %}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ bot.claimsRepeated }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ bot.countermeasures | length }}</td>
    </tr>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tbody></table></div>
<p class="note" style="margin-top:10px">Both figures are the P2 topical-news persona in the market where the
  assistant does worst, with the market named. Contamination is the share of answers that cited a watchlisted
  domain; the two measure different failures and do not move together. Coverage is still thin: a cell below
  n={{ metrics.lowN }} is greyed as low-confidence and shown for transparency, not asserted. We test the
  public consumer interface, not the API. Countermeasures are not yet carried in the published feed and
  show as zero.</p>

<div class="callout" style="margin-top:26px"><b>The rest of this page is a shell.</b> A benchmark issue is one
  cluster over one month, and the full issue is not specified yet. What is settled below is the coverage of
  each issue, the grain-of-truth split, and the A&times;B matrix. Everything per-market lives on the pages
  that own it &mdash; each market and each claim.</div>

<h2 id="issues" style="margin:30px 0 6px">Issues</h2>
<p class="note" style="margin:0 0 14px">One issue per cluster per month. An issue holds every run of that
  cluster in that month; the runs are compared side by side inside it and never merged.</p>
<div class="panel"><table>
  <caption class="visually-hidden">Benchmark issues, newest first</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Issue</th><th scope="col">Cluster</th><th scope="col" class="num">Markets</th>
    <th scope="col" class="num">Claims</th><th scope="col" class="num">Answers</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for issue in benchmarks.issues %}
    <tr><th scope="row" style="font-weight:400"><a href="{{ issue.url | url }}">{{ issue.monthLabel }}</a></th>
      <td style="color:var(--dim)">{{ issue.clusterName }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ issue.markets | length }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ issue.claimsCount }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ issue.responses }}</td></tr>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tbody></table></div>

<h2 id="grain" style="margin:30px 0 6px">The grain-of-truth split</h2>
<p class="note" style="margin:0 0 14px">Claims built on a real event against claims invented outright, by
  question type, {{ benchmarks.claimScopeNote }}. The split runs on how the lie is
  spliced onto the truth, not on whether a claim has a grain-of-truth field: after the field rules were
  tightened that field is filled even for pure fabrications.</p>
<div class="panel"><table>
  <caption class="visually-hidden">Repeat rate on claims built on a real event against pure fabrications, by question type</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">{{ 'col.persona' | t }}</th><th scope="col" class="num">Real event underneath</th>
    <th scope="col" class="num">Invented outright</th><th scope="col">Difference</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for row in benchmarks.grain_of_truth %}
    <tr data-persona="{{ row.persona }}">
      <th scope="row" class="mono" style="font-weight:400;font-size:12px;color:var(--dimmer)">{{ row.persona }} &middot; {{ row.persona | personaLabel }}</th>
      <td class="num">{{ row.with_grain | rate }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ row.pure | rate }}</td>
      <td style="color:var(--dim);font-size:12.5px">{{ "significant" if row.significant else "not significant" }}</td></tr>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tbody></table></div>

<h2 id="abx" style="margin:30px 0 6px">A&times;B matrix</h2>
<p class="note" style="margin:0 0 14px">Every answer {{ benchmarks.claimScopeNote }},
  placed by what the assistant did and whether it cited a listed source.</p>
{% include "partials/abx-matrix.njk" %}

<h2 id="funnel" style="margin:30px 0 6px">From answers to incidents</h2>
<p class="note" style="margin:0 0 14px">Across every run held here. The A&times;B intersection is the filter:
  it is what turns raw source flags into the few cases worth a person's time.</p>
{% include "partials/funnel.njk" %}

<div class="exports" style="margin:26px 0 44px">
  {%- if benchmarks.issues | length %}<a href="{{ '/registry/reports.csv' | url }}">Every metric cell as CSV</a><span>&middot;</span>{% endif %}
  <a href="{{ '/countries/full/' | url }}">The full market breakdown</a><span>&middot;</span>
  <a href="{{ '/data/' | url }}">All exports</a></div>
